      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Luo%2C+X">Xianzhen Luo</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ma%2C+Y">Yingwei Ma</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhu%2C+Q">Qingfu Zhu</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Che%2C+W">Wanxiang Che</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li%2C+B">Binhua Li</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Huang%2C+F">Fei Huang</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li%2C+Y">Yongbin Li</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.23133v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        <span class="search-hit mathjax">Generating</span> and voting multiple answers is an effective method to mitigate reasoning inconsistencies of large language&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.23133v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2506.23133v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.23133v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        <span class="search-hit mathjax">Generating</span> and voting multiple answers is an effective method to mitigate reasoning inconsistencies of large language <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span> (LLMs). Prior works have shown that multiple reasoning formats outperform a single format when <span class="search-hit mathjax">generating</span> multiple answers. However, previous works using multiple formats rely on formats labeled by humans, which could be unsuitable for all tasks and have high labeling costs. To address this issue, we adapt suitable formats to the given tasks by <span class="search-hit mathjax">generating</span> and selecting formats. We first propose how to measure the reasoning error when <span class="search-hit mathjax">generating</span> multiple answers. Then, we introduce Format-Adapter, which utilizes LLMs to <span class="search-hit mathjax">generate</span> and select suitable reasoning formats by minimizing the error measurement we present. We conduct experiments on math and commonsense reasoning tasks, where Format-Adapter achieves a 4.3% performance improvement on average over previous works, demonstrating the effectiveness.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.23133v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2506.23133v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

