      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Iwana%2C+B+K">Brian Kenji Iwana</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.22927v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        <span class="search-hit mathjax">Generative</span> Artificial Intelligence (AI) has rapidly become a powerful tool, capable of&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.22927v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2506.22927v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.22927v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        <span class="search-hit mathjax">Generative</span> Artificial Intelligence (AI) has rapidly become a powerful tool, capable of <span class="search-hit mathjax">generating</span> various types of data, such as images and text. However, despite the significant advancement of <span class="search-hit mathjax">generative</span> AI, time series <span class="search-hit mathjax">generative</span> AI remains underdeveloped, even though the application of time series is essential in finance, climate, and numerous fields. In this research, we propose a novel method of <span class="search-hit mathjax">generating</span> time series conditioned on unstructured natural language descriptions. We use a diffusion <span class="search-hit mathjax">model</span> combined with a language <span class="search-hit mathjax">model</span> to <span class="search-hit mathjax">generate</span> time series from the text. Through the proposed method, we demonstrate that time series <span class="search-hit mathjax">generation</span> based on natural language is possible. The proposed method can provide various applications such as custom forecasting, time series manipulation, data augmentation, and transfer learning. Furthermore, we construct and propose a new public dataset for time series <span class="search-hit mathjax">generation</span>, consisting of 63,010 time series-description pairs.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.22927v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2506.22927v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
